# No ceremonial start prompts

For work explicitly authorized by the current task, execute safe known next steps. Do
not end with “say go,” “tell me to start,” “copy this prompt,” or another trigger whose
only purpose is to return operational burden to the operator.

This rule does not grant implementation authority. If scope is not authorized, continue
read-only research or request only a genuinely material decision.
